-- title:
--   Reduction of an integer modulo 2^n+1 in linear time
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a stack different from `RN`, `RF`, `T1`, `T2`, and let $n\in\mathbb N$ and $z\in\mathbb Z$ with $|z|<2^{2n+1}$. Assume $X$ has $z$ on top (over $L$), `RN` has $2^n$ and `RF` has $2^n+1$ on top. Then `fred X` runs from $s$ to
--   $$s\big[X := (z \bmod (2^n+1)) :: L\big]$$
--   with cost at most $20000\,(n+3)$; the result is the canonical residue in $[0,2^n]$.
--
--   The procedure splits $z$ twice by $2^n$, uses $2^n\equiv-1$ to fold the pieces with additions and a negation, and then applies at most two additions and two subtractions of the modulus. It is the reduction step after every butterfly, twist and untwist in the Fermat ring.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** States are `IState NS` records with item stacks `G : Fin NS → List Item` (head = top), input pointer `ip` and output `out`; `s.upd X L` replaces stack `X` by `L`; `ints A` is the list of integer items of `A`. The named stacks (`ARG`, `PRM`, `RN`, `RF`, `DX`, `DL`, …) are fixed indices in `Fin 32`. `IRuns I iprog p s s' c` means that `p` executes from `s` to exactly `s'` with some cost $c' \le c$, so costs are upper bounds; the program text `iprog` and input `I` are arbitrary unless constrained.
-- source:
--   A. Schönhage, V. Strassen, Schnelle Multiplikation großer Zahlen, Computing 7 (1971), 281–292 (main theorem: O(n log n log log n) multitape TM multiplication). Lemma `NLogN.fred_runs` of the Lean development NLogN/SSBase.lean (lines 229–269), written for the prove2.me integer-multiplication campaign.

